%N A399211 Number of solutions to x^2 + 8*y^2 = n in positive integers x and y.
%H A399211 Seiichi Manyama, <a href="/A399211/b399211.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
%F A399211 G.f.: (theta_3(q) - 1)*(theta_3(q^8) - 1)/4, where theta_3() is the Jacobi theta function. - _Ilya Gutkovskiy_, Sep 03 2026
%o A399211 (PARI) a(n) = if(n==0, 0, sum(k=1, sqrtint((n-1)\8), issquare(n-8*k^2)));
